L:1/8
N:Probably John Eccles 1650-1735, celebrated theatrical/operatic composer.
N:Much less likely to be his father Solomon, also a composer, who became a religious fanatic,
N:nor even his brother Thomas, who despite being "an excellent performer (on the violin) being
N:idle and dissipated, he gained a scanty and precarious subsistence by wandering from tavern to tavern
N:in the city and playing to such of the company as desired to hear him." (Groves 1928)
